{"parents": [], "prev": {"link": "../plugins/", "title": "Plugins"}, "next": {"link": "../base/", "title": "Core"}, "title": "Utilities", "meta": {}, "body": "<section id=\"utilities\">\n<h1>Utilities<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#utilities\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-utilities-event\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorEvent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">value</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">names=&lt;not</span> <span class=\"pre\">given&gt;</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">*values</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">module=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">qualname=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">type=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">start=1</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">boundary=None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/enum.html#enum.Enum\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Enum</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Enum of events that the orchestrator can emit.</p>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_REGISTERED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_REGISTERED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_registered'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_REGISTERED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when an agent is registered. Take the agent name as argument (<cite>agent_name</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_READY\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_READY</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_ready'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_READY\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when an agent is ready. Take the agent name as argument (<cite>agent_name</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_STARTED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_STARTED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_started'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_STARTED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when an agent is started. Take the agent name as argument (<cite>agent_name</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_TERMINATED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_TERMINATED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_terminated'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_TERMINATED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when an agent is terminated. Take the agent name as argument (<cite>agent_name</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_ERROR\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_ERROR</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_error'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_ERROR\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when an agent reports an error. Take the agent name and error message as arguments (<cite>agent_name</cite>, <cite>error_message</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_HEARTBEAT\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_HEARTBEAT</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_heartbeat'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_HEARTBEAT\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when an agent sends a heartbeat signal. Take the agent name as argument (<cite>agent_name</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AgentEvent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">value</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">names=&lt;not</span> <span class=\"pre\">given&gt;</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">*values</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">module=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">qualname=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">type=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">start=1</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">boundary=None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/enum.html#enum.Enum\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Enum</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Enum of events that an agent can emit.</p>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_READY\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_READY</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_ready'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_READY\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is ready to execute. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_START\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_START</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_started'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_START\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is started. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_STOPPED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_STOPPED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_stopped'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_STOPPED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is stopped. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_TERMINATED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_TERMINATED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_terminated'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_TERMINATED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is terminated. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_ERROR\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_ERROR</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_error'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_ERROR\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent encounters an error. Take the error message as argument (<cite>error_message</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_PAUSED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_PAUSED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_paused'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_PAUSED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is paused. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_RESUMED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_RESUMED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_resumed'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_RESUMED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is resumed. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMPLETED\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_COMPLETED</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_completed'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMPLETED\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is completed. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_IDLE\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_IDLE</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_idle'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_IDLE\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is idle. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_WORKING\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_WORKING</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_working'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_WORKING\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is working. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_CLOSE\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_CLOSE</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_close'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_CLOSE\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent is closing. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_MESSAGE\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_MESSAGE</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_message'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_MESSAGE\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent sends a message. Take the message as argument (<cite>message</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_COMMAND</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_command'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent receives a command. Take the command as argument (<cite>command</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_RESPONSE\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_COMMAND_RESPONSE</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_command_response'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_RESPONSE\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent sends a response to a command. Take the response as argument (<cite>response</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_ERROR\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_COMMAND_ERROR</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_command_error'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_ERROR\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent sends an error response to a command. Take the error message as argument (<cite>error_message</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_COMPLETE\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_COMMAND_COMPLETE</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_command_complete'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_COMPLETE\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent sends a completion response to a command. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_START\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_COMMAND_START</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_command_start'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_START\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent starts a command. Take the command as argument (<cite>command</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_STOP\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_COMMAND_STOP</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_command_stop'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_COMMAND_STOP\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent stops a command. Take the command as argument (<cite>command</cite>).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_HEARTBEAT\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AGENT_HEARTBEAT</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'agent_heartbeat'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.AgentEvent.AGENT_HEARTBEAT\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Event emitted when the agent sends a heartbeat signal. Take no arguments.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-utilities-event-manager\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>event_manager module.\nThis module implements the EventManager class for centralized event handling within the application.\nEventManager keeps a dictionary of callbacks (listeners) associated with events identified by their enum member.\nUse this class to:\n- Register unique events and attach callback functions to them.\n- Emit events passing specific parameters and default data (event date and time).\nIt isolates errors in one callback so that they do not affect the execution of others.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">EventManager</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_workers</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">10</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Event manager class.</p>\n<p>Manages the registration, attachment, and emission of events.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>_listeners</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>dict</em></a>) \u2013 A dictionary mapping enum members to lists of callback functions.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_executor</strong> (<em>ThreadPoolExecutor</em>) \u2013 Thread pool for executing callbacks asynchronously.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_shutdown</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>) \u2013 Flag indicating if the event manager is shutting down.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><strong>max_workers</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>Features:</dt><dd><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>register_event: Registers a new event and attaches a callback to it.</p></li>\n<li><p>emit: Emits the event by calling all attached callbacks, including default data such as event date and time.</p></li>\n<li><p>shutdown: Safely shuts down the event manager and its thread pool.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">enum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">Enum</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">EventManager</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Define your events</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">MyEvents</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Enum</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">TASK_STARTED</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;task_started&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">TASK_COMPLETED</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;task_completed&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">TASK_FAILED</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;task_failed&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Create callback functions</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">on_task_started</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"o\">**</span><span class=\"n\">kwargs</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Task </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\"> started at </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">kwargs</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">&#39;event_time&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">on_task_completed</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"o\">**</span><span class=\"n\">kwargs</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Task </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\"> completed with result: </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">on_task_failed</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"o\">**</span><span class=\"n\">kwargs</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Task </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\"> failed with error: </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Initialize the event manager</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">EventManager</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Register events and callbacks</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">register_event</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyEvents</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TASK_STARTED</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">on_task_started</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">register_event</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyEvents</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TASK_COMPLETED</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">on_task_completed</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">register_event</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyEvents</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TASK_FAILED</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">on_task_failed</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Emit events</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyEvents</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TASK_STARTED</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;data_processing&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyEvents</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TASK_COMPLETED</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;data_processing&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;success&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyEvents</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TASK_FAILED</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;data_processing&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;timeout&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Shutdown when done</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">shutdown</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager.register_event\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">register_event</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">callback</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager.register_event\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Registers and attaches a callback to an event.</p>\n<p>If the event is not present, it is automatically registered.\nCallbacks are stored in the order they are added.\nExceptions raised by one callback do not prevent others from executing.</p>\n<p>The listeners are keyed by the enum member itself, so members sharing a\nname across different enums stay independent: a callback registered for\n<cite>AgentEvent.AGENT_ERROR</cite> is not invoked when\n<cite>OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_ERROR</cite> is emitted.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>event</strong> (<em>Enum</em>) \u2013 The Enum member identifying the event.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>callback</strong> (<em>Callable</em>) \u2013 The function to be invoked when the event is emitted.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">register_event</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AgentEvent</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AGENT_START</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">on_agent_started</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager.emit\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">emit</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">args</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager.emit\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Emits an event by invoking all attached callbacks.</p>\n<p>If listeners exist for the event, they are executed asynchronously.\nBefore execution, default data such as the <cite>event_date</cite> and <cite>event_time</cite> are added to kwargs.</p>\n<p>Only the parameters accepted by each callback are passed, via filtering based on the function signature.\nExceptions raised by a callback are caught to avoid interrupting the execution of the others.</p>\n<p>Only the callbacks registered for this exact enum member are invoked.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>event</strong> (<em>Enum</em>) \u2013 The Enum member identifying the event to be emitted.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>*args</strong> \u2013 Positional arguments passed to the callbacks.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>**kwargs</strong> \u2013 Keyword arguments passed to the callbacks.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">event_manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">emit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AgentEvent</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AGENT_START</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">agent_name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Agent_1&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager.shutdown\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">shutdown</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">wait</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager.shutdown\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Shuts down the event manager and thread pool.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>wait</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>) \u2013 If True, waits for all running tasks to complete.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-utilities-messaging\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.now_iso\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">now_iso</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.now_iso\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return current timestamp in ISO format.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.generate_request_id\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">generate_request_id</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.generate_request_id\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Generate a unique request ID.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ServiceMessage</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">sender</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">type</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Literal</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"s\"><span class=\"pre\">'COMMAND'</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\"><span class=\"pre\">'STATUS'</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">payload</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Any</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">timestamp</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">datetime.datetime</span></a></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>sender</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>type</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Literal\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Literal</em></a><em>[</em><em>'COMMAND'</em><em>, </em><em>'STATUS'</em><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>payload</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Any\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Any</em></a><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>timestamp</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>datetime</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.sender\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">sender</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.sender\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.type\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">type</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Literal\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">Literal</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"s\"><span class=\"pre\">'COMMAND'</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\"><span class=\"pre\">'STATUS'</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.type\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.payload\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">payload</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">Dict</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Any\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">Any</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.payload\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.timestamp\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">timestamp</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">datetime</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.timestamp\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.to_dict\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.to_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">object</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.to_json\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_json</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">json_kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.to_json\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return a JSON string representation of the event.</p>\n<p>Passes json_kwargs to json.dumps (e.g. indent=2, ensure_ascii=False).</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.to_bytes\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_bytes</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.to_bytes\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Convert ServiceMessage to bytes for transmission.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Encoded message bytes with newline terminator</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#bytes\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bytes</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.from_bytes\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_bytes</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">raw_bytes</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.from_bytes\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create ServiceMessage from bytes received from transmission.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>raw_bytes</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#bytes\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bytes</em></a>) \u2013 Raw message bytes</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>ServiceMessage instance</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/json.html#json.JSONDecodeError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>json.JSONDecodeError</strong></a> \u2013 If the bytes cannot be decoded as JSON</p></li>\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#KeyError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>KeyError</strong></a> \u2013 If required fields are missing from the envelope</p></li>\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If timestamp cannot be parsed</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.create_command\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">create_command</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">sender</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">command</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">args</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">request_id</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">meta</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.create_command\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create a COMMAND type ServiceMessage.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>sender</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Message sender identifier</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>command</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Command name</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>args</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>list</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional command arguments</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>request_id</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional request identifier</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>meta</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>dict</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional metadata</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>ServiceMessage instance with type=\u201dCOMMAND\u201d</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.create_command_response\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">create_command_response</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">sender</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">status</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">code</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">data</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">request_id</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">error</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.create_command_response\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create a COMMAND type ServiceMessage representing a response.</p>\n<p>The payload follows a standard shape used by the CLI command interface:\n- status: \u201csuccess\u201d or \u201cerror\u201d\n- code: numeric status/code (0 for generic success, or HTTP-like error codes)\n- data: dict with response data when status is \u201csuccess\u201d\n- error: human-readable error string when status is \u201cerror\u201d\n- request_id: correlates this response to the original request\n- protocol_version: the protocol version used by the framework</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>sender</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Message sender identifier (e.g. \u201corchestrator\u201d or \u201ccommand_handler\u201d).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>status</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Literal\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Literal</em></a><em>[</em><em>'success'</em><em>, </em><em>'error'</em><em>]</em>) \u2013 Command status (\u201csuccess\u201d or \u201cerror\u201d).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>code</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Numeric response code (default 0).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>data</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>dict</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional payload data for successful responses.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>request_id</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional request identifier to correlate request/response.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>error</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional error information (string) for error responses.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>ServiceMessage instance with type=\u201dCOMMAND\u201d and a standardized payload.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.create_status\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">create_status</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">sender</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">status</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">error</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">generation_id</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage.create_status\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create a STATUS type ServiceMessage.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>sender</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Message sender identifier</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>status</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Status message content</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>data</strong> \u2013 Optional additional data to include in the status message</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>error</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>generation_id</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>ServiceMessage instance with type=\u201dSTATUS\u201d</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">MessageChannel</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">a_type</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">zmq_address</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'tcp://127.0.0.1:5555'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>A message channel for communication between agents and orchestrators.</p>\n<p>Provides a unified interface for sending and receiving messages across different\ncommunication protocols including thread queues, process queues, and ZeroMQ sockets.\nThe channel automatically handles the underlying communication mechanism based on the\nspecified type, allowing seamless communication between system components.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>a_type</strong> \u2013 The type of communication channel (\u2018thread\u2019, \u2018process\u2019, \u2018zmq_router\u2019, or \u2018zmq_dealer\u2019).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>zmq_address</strong> \u2013 ZeroMQ address (only used for ZMQ types, e.g., \u2018<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"tcp://127.0.0.1:5555\">tcp://127.0.0.1:5555</a>\u2019).</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>a_type</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Literal\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Literal</em></a><em>[</em><em>'thread'</em><em>, </em><em>'process'</em><em>, </em><em>'zmq_router'</em><em>, </em><em>'zmq_dealer'</em><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>zmq_address</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Server mode (orchestrator)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">server</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">MessageChannel</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">&#39;zmq_router&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s1\">&#39;tcp://*:5555&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">msg</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">ServiceMessage</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">&#39;agent1&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s1\">&#39;STATUS&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s1\">&#39;running&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">datetime</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">now</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">server</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">send</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">&#39;target&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">received</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">server</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">receive</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">timeout</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Client mode (CLI/web service)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">client</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">MessageChannel</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">&#39;zmq_dealer&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s1\">&#39;tcp://127.0.0.1:5555&#39;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">response</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">client</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">send_and_receive</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">timeout</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">5.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">client</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.send\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">send</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">target</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">msg</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.send\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Send a message through the communication channel.</p>\n<p>Sends a ServiceMessage through the appropriate communication mechanism based on\nthe channel type. For thread/process queues, the message is queued directly.\nFor ZMQ sockets, the message is sent as JSON frames.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>target</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 The intended recipient identifier. For ZMQ ROUTER, this is used\nfor routing. For queues, it\u2019s ignored.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>msg</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a>) \u2013 The ServiceMessage instance to send containing sender, type, payload,\nand timestamp information.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.receive\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">receive</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">timeout</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.receive\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Receive a message from the communication channel.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Maximum time in seconds to wait for a message. If None, the\ncall may block indefinitely for queue-based channels or use the\ndefault blocking behaviour for ZMQ sockets.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>A ServiceMessage if one was received, None if no message is available or\ntimeout was reached.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.send_and_receive\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">send_and_receive</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">msg</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">timeout</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">5.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">auto_close</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.send_and_receive\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Send a message and wait for response (dealer mode only).</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>msg</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a>) \u2013 ServiceMessage to send.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum time to wait for response in seconds.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>auto_close</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>) \u2013 Whether to close the connection after receiving response.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>ServiceMessage response if successful, None otherwise.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.close\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">close</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel.close\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Close the message channel and cleanup resources.</p>\n<p>For ZMQ channels, closes the socket and terminates the context.\nFor thread/process queues, no cleanup is necessary.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-utilities-command-handler\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Command Handler for PyOrchestrate CLI Interface</p>\n<p>This module contains the CommandHandler class which processes external CLI commands\nand provides structured responses. This separates command handling logic from the\ncore Orchestrator functionality.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CommandPermissions</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Command permissions management for PyOrchestrate CLI interface.</p>\n<p>Provides predefined permission sets for different environments and\nutilities for command filtering.</p>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.ALL_COMMANDS\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ALL_COMMANDS</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">{'commands',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'dependencies',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history-stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'ps',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'shutdown',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'start',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'status',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'stop'}</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.ALL_COMMANDS\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.PRODUCTION\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PRODUCTION</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">{'commands',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'dependencies',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history-stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'ps',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'status'}</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.PRODUCTION\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.DEVELOPMENT\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DEVELOPMENT</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">{'commands',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'dependencies',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history-stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'ps',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'shutdown',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'start',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'status',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'stop'}</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.DEVELOPMENT\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.READ_ONLY\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">READ_ONLY</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">{'commands',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'dependencies',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history-stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'ps',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'status'}</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.READ_ONLY\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.MONITORING\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">MONITORING</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">{'commands',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'history-stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'ps',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'stats',</span> <span class=\"pre\">'status'}</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.MONITORING\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.validate_commands\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">validate_commands</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">commands</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.validate_commands\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Validate and filter out unknown commands.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>commands</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Set</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 Set of command names to validate</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Set of valid commands</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Set</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.get_preset\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_preset</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">preset_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandPermissions.get_preset\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get a predefined permission set.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>preset_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the preset (production, development, read_only, monitoring)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Set of allowed commands</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If preset_name is not recognized</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Set</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py exception\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandException\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CommandException</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">message</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">code</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandException\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#Exception\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Exception</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Custom exception for command handling errors.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>message</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>code</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandHandler\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CommandHandler</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">orchestrator</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">allowed_commands</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandHandler\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Handles external CLI commands for the orchestrator.</p>\n<p>This class processes commands received from the CLI interface and returns\nstructured responses. It keeps the command logic separate from the core\norchestrator functionality.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>orchestrator</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../orchestrator/#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator\"><em>Orchestrator</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>allowed_commands</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>set</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>] </em><em>| </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandHandler.execute_command\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">execute_command</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">command</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">args</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandHandler.execute_command\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Execute external commands and return structured responses.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>command</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>args</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>list</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">dict</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandHandler.execute_command_msg\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">execute_command_msg</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">request_msg</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.command_handler.CommandHandler.execute_command_msg\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Execute a command from a ServiceMessage and return a ServiceMessage response.</p>\n<p>This is a non-breaking wrapper that allows callers to pass the full\nrequest <cite>ServiceMessage</cite> and receive a fully-formed <cite>ServiceMessage</cite>\nresponse (success or error). It uses the existing <cite>execute_command</cite>\nimplementation internally.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>request_msg</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-utilities-validation\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ValidationSeverity</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">value</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">names=&lt;not</span> <span class=\"pre\">given&gt;</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">*values</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">module=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">qualname=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">type=None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">start=1</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">boundary=None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/enum.html#enum.Enum\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Enum</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Severity levels for validation errors.</p>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity.WARNING\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">WARNING</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'warning'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity.WARNING\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity.ERROR\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ERROR</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'error'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity.ERROR\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity.CRITICAL\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CRITICAL</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'critical'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity.CRITICAL\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ValidationResult</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">field</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">message</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">''</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">severity</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">ValidationSeverity.ERROR</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Represents the result of a single validation check.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>field</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>message</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>severity</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationSeverity\"><em>ValidationSeverity</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py exception\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ConfigValidationError\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ConfigValidationError</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">message</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">config_class</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">''</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ConfigValidationError\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#Exception\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Exception</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Base exception for configuration validation errors.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>message</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>results</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\"><em>ValidationResult</em></a><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>config_class</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py exception\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ConfigValidationWarning\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ConfigValidationWarning</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">message</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">config_class</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">''</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ConfigValidationWarning\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#Warning\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Warning</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Warning for configuration validation issues that don\u2019t block execution.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>message</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>results</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\"><em>ValidationResult</em></a><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>config_class</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationPolicy\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ValidationPolicy</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">ignore_warnings</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">ignore_errors</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationPolicy\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Policy that determines when to raise an exception on validation failures.</p>\n<p>The validation policy determines how to handle errors and warnings during validation:</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>If <cite>ignore_warnings</cite> is True: warnings are logged as ConfigValidationWarning (logged but don\u2019t block execution)</p></li>\n<li><p>If <cite>ignore_warnings</cite> is False: warnings are treated as errors (<cite>ConfigValidationError</cite>, blocking execution)</p></li>\n<li><p>If <cite>ignore_errors</cite> is True: errors are completely ignored</p></li>\n<li><p>If <cite>ignore_errors</cite> is False: errors raise <cite>ConfigValidationError</cite> (blocking execution)</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Critical errors (CRITICAL) always raise <cite>ConfigValidationError</cite>, regardless of the policy settings.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>ignore_warnings</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>ignore_errors</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationPolicy.should_raise\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">should_raise</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationPolicy.should_raise\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Determine what kind of exception should be raised based on validation results and policy.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>results</strong> (<em>List</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\"><em>ValidationResult</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 List of validation results.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>\u201cerror\u201d if a ConfigValidationError should be raised</p></li>\n<li><p>\u201dwarning\u201d if a ConfigValidationWarning should be raised</p></li>\n<li><p>None if no exception should be raised</p></li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Optional[Literal[\u201cerror\u201d, \u201cwarning\u201d]]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-utilities-periodic-timer\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>A module providing a PeriodicTimer class to manage periodic execution intervals with optional\ncompensation for accumulated delays. This is particularly useful in scenarios where tasks\nneed to be executed at consistent intervals, such as in real-time processing, polling mechanisms,\nor scheduling repeated tasks.</p>\n<p>The PeriodicTimer class encapsulates the logic for calculating sleep times between iterations,\nhandling compensations for any delays that may occur during task execution to maintain the\ndesired frequency of execution.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-python notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">datetime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">datetime</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">threading</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">PeriodicTimer</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">periodic_task</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">now</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">datetime</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">now</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">timestamp</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">now</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">strftime</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;%H:%M:%S.</span><span class=\"si\">%f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)[:</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Task executed at </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">timestamp</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"n\">stop_event</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">threading</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Event</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">timer</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">PeriodicTimer</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">interval</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">compensate_delay</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">False</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">while</span> <span class=\"ow\">not</span> <span class=\"n\">stop_event</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">is_set</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">periodic_task</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">timer</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wait</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stop_event</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n            <span class=\"k\">break</span>\n<span class=\"k\">except</span> <span class=\"ne\">KeyboardInterrupt</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">stop_event</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer.PeriodicTimer\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PeriodicTimer</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">interval</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">compensate_delay</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer.PeriodicTimer\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Manages periodic execution intervals with optional delay compensation.</p>\n<p>The PeriodicTimer class is designed to facilitate the execution of tasks at consistent\nintervals. It calculates the appropriate sleep time between iterations and can optionally\ncompensate for any delays that occur during task execution to maintain the desired\nfrequency.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>interval</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 The time interval in seconds between each iteration.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>compensate_delay</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>) \u2013 Determines whether to compensate for accumulated delays.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>next_time</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 The scheduled start time for the next iteration.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>interval</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>compensate_delay</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer.PeriodicTimer.wait\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">wait</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">stop_event</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer.PeriodicTimer.wait\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Calculates the remaining sleep time and pauses the thread accordingly.</p>\n<p>This method determines how long the current thread should sleep to maintain the\ndesired interval between task executions. If <cite>compensate_delay</cite> is enabled and\nthe thread is running behind schedule, it adjusts the next scheduled time to\nprevent delays from accumulating over iterations.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>stop_event</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/threading.html#threading.Event\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>threading.Event</em></a><em> | </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/multiprocessing.html#multiprocessing.Event\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>multiprocessing.Event</em></a>) \u2013 An event used to signal the thread to stop waiting\nand terminate the loop. If the event is set during the wait period, the\nmethod returns immediately.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>Returns True if the <cite>stop_event</cite> was set during the wait, indicating</dt><dd><p>that the loop should terminate. Returns False otherwise.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-python notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">threading</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">periodic_timer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">PeriodicTimer</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">stop_event</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">threading</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Event</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"n\">timer</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">PeriodicTimer</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">interval</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">2.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">timer</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wait</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stop_event</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Stop event detected. Exiting loop.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Continuing to next iteration.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer.PeriodicTimer.reset\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">reset</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.periodic_timer.PeriodicTimer.reset\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Resets the timer to the current time.</p>\n<p>This method reinitializes the <cite>next_time</cite> attribute to the current high-resolution\ncounter, effectively resetting the timer\u2019s schedule. This can be useful if the\ntiming sequence needs to be restarted without waiting for the next interval.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-utilities-logguru\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>This module defines the <cite>LoggerFactory</cite> class, which creates and manages\ncustom loggers built on Loguru.</p>\n<p><strong>Loguru</strong> is a Python logging library that considerably simplifies log\nhandling. One of its core concepts is the <em>sink</em>, a destination for log\nmessages such as a file, the console or another stream. Sinks define where and\nhow messages are emitted, and support features like file rotation,\ncompression, filters and custom formatting.</p>\n<p><cite>LoggerFactory</cite> uses those concepts to:</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>Remove the default logger and add a console sink with a specific format.</p></li>\n<li><p>Manage individual file sinks per log identifier, with rotation and\ncompression.</p></li>\n<li><p>Provide a thread-safe way to create and retrieve loggers configured for the\ndifferent components of an application.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">LoggerFactory</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Factory that creates and manages custom loggers using Loguru.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>_sinks</strong> (<em>Dict</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 Map of sink IDs.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_initialized</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>) \u2013 Whether the logger has been initialized.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_lock</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/threading.html#threading.Lock\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>threading.Lock</em></a>) \u2013 Lock guaranteeing thread-safe access to sinks.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>rotation_default</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Default rotation frequency for log files.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>retention_default</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Default retention period for log files.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>compression_default</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Default compression type for log files.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>log_path_default</strong> (<em>Path</em><em> | </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Default directory for log files.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.prod_format\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">prod_format</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'&lt;green&gt;{time:YYYY-MM-DD</span> <span class=\"pre\">HH:mm:ss.SSS}&lt;/green&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">|</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;level&gt;{level:</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;8}&lt;/level&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">|</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;level&gt;&lt;cyan&gt;{name}&lt;/cyan&gt;:&lt;cyan&gt;{function}&lt;/cyan&gt;:&lt;cyan&gt;{line}&lt;/cyan&gt;&lt;/level&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">-</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;level&gt;{elapsed}&lt;/level&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">|</span> <span class=\"pre\">{extra[name]}</span> <span class=\"pre\">|</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;level&gt;{message}&lt;/level&gt;'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.prod_format\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.dev_format\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">dev_format</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'&lt;green&gt;{time:YYYY-MM-DD</span> <span class=\"pre\">HH:mm:ss.SSS}&lt;/green&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">|</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;level&gt;{level:</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;8}&lt;/level&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">|</span> <span class=\"pre\">{extra[name]}</span> <span class=\"pre\">|</span> <span class=\"pre\">&lt;level&gt;{message}&lt;/level&gt;'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.dev_format\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.rotation_default\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation_default</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'00:00'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.rotation_default\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.retention_default\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">retention_default</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'7</span> <span class=\"pre\">days'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.retention_default\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.compression_default\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">compression_default</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'zip'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.compression_default\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.log_path_default\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">log_path_default</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Path</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.log_path_default\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.set_defaults\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">set_defaults</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">retention</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">compression</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">log_path</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.set_defaults\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Sets the default values for rotation, retention, compression and log_path.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>rotation</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>retention</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>compression</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>log_path</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>Path</em><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.create_logger\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">create_logger</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">log_identifier</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">logger_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">level</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'INFO'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">retention</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">compression</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">log_path</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.create_logger\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Creates a new <cite>logger</cite>, or returns an existing one.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>log_identifier</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Unique identifier for the logger (for example\nthe <cite>thread</cite> name).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>logger_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Logger name, included in the message format.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>level</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Log level.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>rotation</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Rotation frequency for log files.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>retention</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Retention period for log files.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>compression</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Compression type for log files.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>log_path</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>Path</em>) \u2013 Directory where log files are written.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The configured logger.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.close_all\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">close_all</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.utilities.logguru.LoggerFactory.close_all\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Closes every <cite>sink</cite>.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n</section>\n", "metatags": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n", "rellinks": [["genindex", "General Index", "I", "index"], ["py-modindex", "Python Module Index", "", "modules"], ["base", "Core", "N", "next"], ["plugins", "Plugins", "P", "previous"]], "sourcename": "utilities.rst.txt", "toc": "<ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#\">Utilities</a><ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event\">PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event</a><ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorEvent</span></code></a><ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_REGISTERED\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_REGISTERED</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_READY\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorEvent.